card.statement:
Let $n$ be a positive integer, $\K$ a field, and $(q_1,\ldots,q_n)\in(\K\setminus\{0,1\})^n$. Then the skew fields of fractions of the following three algebras are isomorphic:

[(i)]

- The tensor product of quantum Weyl algebras

\begin{equation}
A_1^{q_1}(\K)\otimes_\K \cdots \otimes_\K A_1^{q_n}(\K);
\end{equation}

- The tensor product of quantum planes

\begin{equation}
\mathcal{O}_{q_1}(\Bbbk^2)\otimes_\K\cdots\otimes_\K
\mathcal{O}_{q_n}(\Bbbk^2);
\end{equation}

- The multiparameter quantized Weyl algebra

\begin{equation}
A_n^{\bar q,\La}(\K)
\end{equation}

with parameters $\bar q = (q_1,\ldots,q_n)$, and $\La=(\la_{ij})$, $\la_{ij}=1$ for all $i,j=1,\ldots,n$.
